{"source_key":"sha256-1b040a14b56f8e8c10dd28d48155f19f","record_index":313,"record_hash":"sha256:212d8a4dbce21d671dc2145eaaf25c90eb0086a9e2ab7f00ea00c2520a98c777","timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:14:44.979Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"user","text":"<subagent_notification>\n{\"agent_path\":\"[REDACTED:entropy]\",\"status\":{\"completed\":\"**Bottom Line**\\n`caleb/single-branch-project-starting` adds the backend/UI path for metadata-only project init, but it does not touch `crates/but`. CLI setup still means “enter managed workspace mode.”\\n\\n**1. Current CLI Commands**\\n- `but setup`: the only explicit CLI project add/setup command. It registers the repo, picks/configures a target, creates `gb-local` if needed, calls legacy `set_base_branch`, switches to `gitbutler/workspace`, and installs managed hooks. See [args](<[REDACTED:path]>), [handler](<[REDACTED:path]>), and [setup::repo](<[REDACTED:path]>).\\n- `but setup --init`: same, but first creates a Git repo and empty initial commit when none exists. See [find_or_initialize_repo](<[REDACTED:path]>).\\n- `but gui [path]` only opens the app URL; it does not add/init a project in CLI code. See [GUI handler](<[REDACTED:path]>).\\n- Other commands go through `setup::init_ctx`; if the repo is missing project/setup state, it prompts to run the same managed setup. See [init_ctx](<[REDACTED:path]>) and [prompt text](<[REDACTED:path]>).\\n- `but agent setup` also checks project setup and can call the same legacy setup routine. See [agent setup check](<[REDACTED:path]>) and [run_but_setup](<[REDACTED:path]>).\\n\\n**2. Likely Change Points**\\n- [crates/but/src/args/mod.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): add CLI option(s) to `Setup`.\\n- [crates/but/src/lib.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): route `setup` into managed vs single-branch setup.\\n- [crates/but/src/command/legacy/setup.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): add a metadata-only sibling path that reuses remote/target discovery but does not call `set_base_branch_with_perm`, `switch_back_to_workspace_with_perm`, or install hooks.\\n- [crates/but/src/command/legacy/setup.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): `check_project_setup` currently rejects non-`gitbutler/*` branches, so single-branch-ready CLI must relax this when project metadata is present.\\n- [crates/but/src/setup.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): prompt copy still promises switching to `gitbutler/workspace`.\\n- [crates/but/src/command/agent/mod.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>): decide whether `but agent setup` follows the same mode.\\n- [crates/but/skill/](<[REDACTED:path]>): update bundled CLI docs after changing workflow.\\n\\nUse the branch’s new helper, not new core logic: [but_workspace::init::set_target_ref_and_init_project](<[REDACTED:path]>) and API wrapper [set_target_ref_and_init_project](<[REDACTED:path]>). `but` already depends on `but-workspace`, so the CLI can call the lower helper while holding its existing lock.\\n\\n**3. Existing Coverage**\\n- CLI setup snapshots: [crates/but/tests/but/command/setup.rs](<[REDACTED:path]>) covers no remote, `gb-local`, non-standard branch, remote HEAD fallback, existing target, JSON output, `--init`, and stale `projects.json`.\\n- Journey test: [from_empty](<[REDACTED:path]>) covers empty dir -> `setup --init` -> repeat `setup` -> `status`.\\n- New branch backend coverage: [workspace init tests](<[REDACTED:path]>) cover keeping current branch, no workspace ref, target commit behavior, push remote preservation, and error cases.\\n- API tests: [workspace.rs tests](<[REDACTED:path]>) cover remote target acceptance, local branch rejection, and merge-base target id.\\n- UI e2e: [[REDACTED:entropy].spec.ts](<[REDACTED:path]>) verifies adding a project leaves the user on the current branch and creates no workspace ref.\\n- Missing: no `crates/but` CLI single-branch setup tests yet. `git diff origin/master...caleb/single-branch-project-starting -- crates/but` is empty.\\n\\n**4. Minimal CLI Behavior**\\nI’d ship the smallest surface:\\n\\n`but setup --single-branch [--init] [--target <remote/branch>]`\\n\\nBehavior:\\n- registers/adds the project like today;\\n- initializes repo on `--init` like today;\\n- chooses target from `--target` or the existing remote HEAD/main/master heuristic;\\n- creates `gb-local` when there is no push remote, same as today;\\n- writes target metadata via `but_workspace::init::set_target_ref_and_init_project`;\\n- leaves HEAD, worktree, uncommitted changes, hooks, and `[REDACTED:entropy]` alone;\\n- keeps JSON target output compatible unless a caller needs an explicit `mode`.\\n\\nSkipped: a new `but project add` command and a broad `--mode` enum. Add those only when there is a second real setup mode beyond “managed workspace” and “single branch.”\\n\\nNo files edited; no tests run. Read-only investigation only.\\n\\n\"}}\n<[REDACTED:path]>","prompt_source":"system_injected","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:14:44.979Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"}}}}